### Worked example: a record with a compact constructor

```java
record Name(String value) {
    Name {
        value = value.trim().toLowerCase();
        if (value.isEmpty()) throw new IllegalArgumentException();
    }
}
```

The compact constructor is part of the canonical construction path. The goal is to ensure every successfully constructed instance satisfies the same representation rule.

This is different from mutable setters: callers cannot bypass construction by simply assigning to a record component.

